From a0996e3c5c6ada41b1f4fc680d41c5e4c8a7776e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zonglvye <zonglvye@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:54:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 77/91] feat(visualizer): let per-song random pick from a
 chosen pool of styles
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Brings over upstream v0.7.22's 'random lyric style scope' (#771). The core is
small: a pool of built-in styles, stored as JSON, normalised on every read, and
one pick per song that avoids repeating the current one.

- utils/randomVisualizerModes.ts: normalise (built-ins only, deduped, in the
  builtin order, empty pool falls back to all) and pick (never the current style
  when another choice exists)
- useVisualizerSettingsStore: randomVisualizerModes + handleSetRandomVisualizerModes;
  handleSetVisualizerMode now turns per-song random off when a style is chosen by
  hand, unless the caller passes preserveRandom (which the pick itself does) —
  without that, a random pick would switch its own feature off
- useRandomVisualizerMode: replaced with upstream's version - one choice per
  song, no reroll for refreshed metadata or StrictMode, and editing the pool only
  replaces a style that is no longer in it
- panelTab/controls/RandomLyricStylePool: the pool editor, written against the
  player panel's own primitives instead of upstream's settings kit. Lives under
  the style stepper on the 控制 page.

Verified on the device: removing the current style from the pool rerolls it
without switching random off, and advancing a track rotated fume -> partita with
random still on.
